pos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5193905847","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5193905847","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5193905847,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNZS2tw","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T15:38:56Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T15:38:56Z","body":"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a48b383f-0aff-4b85-bf5d-46dd8ed72929\n\n`Viewport::_update_canvas_items()` is called continuously, which should normally be triggered by input events.\n\n> Is it possible to reproduce it with MRP which can be run as a game? \n\nThat doesn't seem to work; it appears to be related to the editor environment. It's easy to reproduce in the editor, but it doesn't trigger when I open the editor settings using the project manager, even though I specified `--rendering-method forward_plus`.\n\n> Considering that it seems to happen only in Sway, and only with certain settings, makes me wonder if that change just uncovered a pre-existing bug. Either with Godot or Sway itself.\n\nThat might be the case.\nI previously noticed that the scan/import progress bar (when tiling) would also lag when its width was insufficient (half of my screen width of 1920).","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5193905847/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5193954002","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5193954002","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5193954002,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNZVy0g","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T15:43:08Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T15:43:08Z","body":"From what I see is that entire `SceneTree::_physics_process()` has exploded in time. Could be something about that window is being squished into smaller than minimum size space, and it tries to resolve it. Or that elements are not pleased with their layout and every single notification it tries to change the layout. Does window size differ between different tiling WMs, which worked and didn't? Have you tried to see the performance if the window is very large (full screen or almost full screen)? `_update_canvas_items` is recursively called, and `update_canvas_items` (no underscore) is only called once viewport size is set (in `_set_size`). And there are plenty of other calls which take up more time than it should. It's probably easier for you to reproduce in editor because it has more complex UI which takes longer to calculate.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5193954002/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194030765","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5194030765","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5194030765,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNZaerQ","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-05T15:49:59Z","updated_at":"2026-08-05T16:00:48Z","body":"> Have you tried to see the performance if the window is very large (full screen or almost full screen)?\n\nThis doesn't work for this issue, but it does work for the import/scan progress bar. However, switching to a floating window works.\n\n> It's probably easier for you to reproduce in editor because it has more complex UI which takes longer to calculate.\n\nAfter waiting 30 seconds for execution, the new breakpoint still indicates that the code is being called. It appears to be in an infinite recursion. \n\nHowever, increasing the width seems to allow it to break out of the infinite recursion. However, it still lags.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5194030765/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5202291218","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5202291218","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5202291218,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNhSqEg","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T08:31:31Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T08:36:41Z","body":"I have tested it all the various combinations of WM/DMs (Plasma on Wayland, Plasma on X11, Sway, Hyprland), command-line options (forward_plus, gl_compatibility, x11, wayland), and have finally managed to reproduce the bug. The performance issues only arise in Wayland tiling WMs (Sway and Hyprland) if Godot is run using X11 display server. Rendering method did not influence results, or only by an insignificant amount. On both tiling WMs, in Godot v4.7, the loading is way way slower when running Godot using X11 display server, but once it loads, the performance is fine. On master, the entire UI is forever slow disregarding if there is a dialog or no. I'll look more into it today.\n\nEdit: Just tested i3, and I can reproduce the bug there too, so it is not exclusively Wayland tiling WM bug.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5202291218/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5202975709","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5202975709","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5202975709,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNh8b3Q","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T09:43:13Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T09:43:13Z","body":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/51105ccbe58381774ecd7a7486d564b202a5192e/main/main.cpp#L5012-L5024\n\nIt seems to be stuck here. This code takes around 1000ms to execute when there is keyboard/mouse input in the dialog window. `scaled_step` is close to `1.0`. \n\nThe values ​​appear normal when there is no keyboard or mouse input.\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/main/main.cpp b/main/main.cpp\nindex dfdac13e7e..6bb46294d3 100644\n--- a/main/main.cpp\n+++ b/main/main.cpp\n@@ -5016,6 +5016,8 @@ bool Main::iteration() {\n        t[t_count++] = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\n        if (wants_present || has_pending_resources_for_processing) {\n                wants_present |= force_redraw_requested;\n+               print_line(scaled_step, process_step, time_scale);\n+               uint64_t t0 = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\n                if ((!force_redraw_requested) && OS::get_singleton()->is_in_low_processor_usage_mode()) {\n                        if (RenderingServer::get_singleton()->has_changed()) {\n                                RenderingServer::get_singleton()->draw(wants_present, scaled_step); // flush visual commands\n@@ -5026,6 +5028,8 @@ bool Main::iteration() {\n                        Engine::get_singleton()->increment_frames_drawn();\n                        force_redraw_requested = false;\n                }\n+               uint64_t t1 = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\n+               print_line(scaled_step, t1-t0, process_step, time_scale);\n        }\n        t[t_count++] = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_msec();\n        process_ticks = OS::get_singleton()->get_ticks_usec() - process_begin;\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\n1.002124 0.13545733333333 1.0\n1.002124 989 0.13545733333333 1.0\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5202975709/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203163208","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5203163208","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5203163208,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNiH4SA","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T10:02:44Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T10:06:35Z","body":"Well, I can reproduce the performance hit, but for me it is not related to dialogs. And most performance costs are going to come from drawing or resizing, which causes excessive drawing. Is there any more action involved to trigger specifically for dialogs? Which dialogs work, and which don't? Is project/editor settings with advanced settings on?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203163208/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203326300","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5203326300","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5203326300,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNiR1XA","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T10:18:04Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T10:29:09Z","body":"Okay, I have managed to fix constant bad performance in the editor by applying PR #121820, which prevents sizing getting out of sync. Now I can reproduce ~3 second spikes when clicking elements in Project Settings.\n\nEdit: I can reproduce the spikes, albeit smaller, by clicking scene nodes in the scene tree.\nEdit 2: The Project Settings performance spike happens if the Project Settings UI does not fit into the window. Resizing the Project Settings window to make it larger fixes the performance. Tested with both advanced settings on and off.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203326300/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203495393","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5203495393","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5203495393,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNicJ4Q","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-06T10:33:25Z","updated_at":"2026-08-06T11:48:26Z","body":"> Is there any more action involved to trigger specifically for dialogs? \n\nSway 1.9, --rendering-method forward_plus/mobile, Xwayland. \n\nKeyboard input or mouse scrolling. These two types of input provide clear visual feedback.\n\n> Which dialogs work, and which don't? \n\nAny dialog opens tiled by default, almost all. Except for the native OS file manager.\n\n> Is project/editor settings with advanced settings on?\n\nThe issue can be reproduced with a new project using default settings (after deleting `~/.config/godot/`, `~/.cache/godot`, and `~/.local/share/godot/`). \n\nThe issue can also be reproduced using the latest build from Actions. https://github.com/godotengine/godot/actions/runs/31017424673\n\nGodot v4.8.dev.mono (51105ccbe) - Linux Mint 22.2 (Zara) on Wayland - X11 display driver, Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - integrated Intel(R) HD Graphics 630 (KBL GT2) - Intel(R) Core(TM) i5-7300HQ CPU @ 2.50GHz (4 threads) - 23.37 GiB memory - PulseAudio (44100 Hz, Stereo/mono)\n\nIt is also worth noting that the main window functions correctly when the width is sufficient. However, when the width is insufficient, the scanning progress bar and the notification message popup in the bottom-right corner both stutter. This may be a separate issue.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5203495393/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5214757346","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5214757346","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5214757346,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNtLh4g","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T08:38:58Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T09:26:15Z","body":"The 3 second slowdown comes from trying to resize a window around 6 times, each time getting delayed by 500 ms. Removing delay here stops the big lag spike, and also it fixes slow dialogs when launching Godot editor or loading scenes. Resize size mismatch delay was here since introduction of DisplayServerX11, and it mainly affects tiling WMs. I have tweaked my existing PR #121820 to fix this. You can try it and see how it works for you.\n\nhttps://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/51105ccbe58381774ecd7a7486d564b202a5192e/platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp#L2778-L2787\n\nThere are a few menus in Project Settings (e.g. Application/Config or GDScript), which take a bit of time to load, around 100-200 ms. That's way better than before. And this 100-200 ms lag for some Project Settings happens in Wayland too, and on floating window managers too (tested Plasma on Wayland). This small spike is not reproducible in 4.7, but reproducible in master. It looks like a different bug.\n\nEdit: Tested \"100-200 ms lag\" for some Project Settings menus with `production=yes`, and with compile optimization I can't reproduce that delay. So it's not another bug, and all is good.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5214757346/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5215066471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5215066471","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5215066471,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNteZZw","user":{"login":"Rindbee","id":30386067,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwMzg2MDY3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/30386067?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee","html_url":"https://github.com/Rindbee","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Rindbee/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:03:46Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T09:03:46Z","body":"```\nWARNING: Resizing window to requested size has failed.\n     at: window_set_size (platform/linuxbsd/x11/display_server_x11.cpp:2783)\n```\n\nI downloaded and tested it from the artifacts. Everything looks fine, except that the warning messages mentioned above are output multiple times when launching the editor.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5215066471/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5215139679","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/122077#issuecomment-5215139679","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/122077","id":5215139679,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNti3Xw","user":{"login":"ELginas","id":42967362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQyOTY3MzYy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/42967362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas","html_url":"https://github.com/ELginas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ELginas/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-07T09:11:21Z","updated_at":"2026-08-07T09:11:21Z","body":"Yup, I am aware of it. I left it up to maintainers to d